1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,401
The first time the Bible says finished, nothing

2
00:00:02,421 --> 00:00:03,061
was broken yet.

3
00:00:03,561 --> 00:00:05,461
Thus the heavens and the earth were finished,

4
00:00:05,941 --> 00:00:07,022
and all the host of them.

5
00:00:07,062 --> 00:00:07,902
Creation complete.

6
00:00:08,462 --> 00:00:09,042
God rested.

7
00:00:09,742 --> 00:00:11,123
He does not leave work half done.

8
00:00:12,463 --> 00:00:14,624
When sin wrecked that world, the Son came down

9
00:00:14,684 --> 00:00:15,144
to mend it.

10
00:00:15,964 --> 00:00:18,524
The Bible says of Jesus: All things were made

11
00:00:18,584 --> 00:00:18,985
by him.

12
00:00:19,165 --> 00:00:21,285
The hands that finished creation came to finish

13
00:00:21,325 --> 00:00:21,765
redemption.

14
00:00:22,705 --> 00:00:24,106
Before the cross, he prayed.

15
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:27,547
I have glorified thee on the earth: I have

16
00:00:27,607 --> 00:00:30,087
finished the work which thou gavest me to do.

17
00:00:30,347 --> 00:00:31,308
He carried it to the end.

18
00:00:31,828 --> 00:00:33,988
When Jesus therefore had received the vinegar,

19
00:00:34,028 --> 00:00:37,969
he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head,

20
00:00:38,729 --> 00:00:39,770
and gave up the ghost.

21
00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:40,730
Two finished works.

22
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:42,230
One Workman.

23
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:44,791
He finished creation, and rested.

24
00:00:45,651 --> 00:00:47,972
He finished redemption, and rested in the tomb

25
00:00:48,092 --> 00:00:48,732
through the sabbath.

26
00:00:49,712 --> 00:00:51,492
And on the first day, morning came.

27
00:00:51,572 --> 00:00:52,733
You were never asked to finish it.

28
00:00:53,233 --> 00:00:54,413
You are asked to rest in it.

29
00:00:54,533 --> 00:00:56,334
He bowed his head so you could lift yours.

30
00:00:56,534 --> 00:00:57,314
The work is finished.

31
00:00:58,314 --> 00:00:59,034
Enter his rest.
